id: pm-9j2r3b
title: "Branch merge is an unrecorded mutation: the field-aware merge produces an item state that no history entry ever produced, so the merged state is unaddressable by restore and point-in-time reads"
description: "The field-aware merge driver converges item files correctly but writes no history entry for the resolution it computed, so the surviving item state has no address in the append-only record.\n\nLive reproduction on 2026.7.25 in a throwaway git repository with pm merge install applied:\n\n  base commit: item created, then updated (stream length 2)\n  branch agent-a: comment_add, update (status in_progress), note_add   -> stream length 5\n  branch agent-b: comment_add, update (priority 1), learnings_add      -> stream length 5\n  git merge agent-a into agent-b\n\nConvergence is good and should be recorded as such: zero conflict markers under .agents/pm, the stream unions to 8 entries with no cross-author loss, the merged item keeps status in_progress from A and priority 1 from B, and all annotations from both branches survive. Point-in-time addressing of pre-divergence versions is stable: pm get --at 2 returns the same state before and after the merge.\n\nThe integrity hole is the merged state itself:\n\n  pm history <id> --verify -> ok false, verify_failed:current_item_hash_mismatch,\n      latest_after_hash f0dfb167..., current_item_hash 917a2941..., current_matches_latest false\n  pm validate            -> validate_history_drift_hash_mismatches:1, history_drift warn, ok true\n  pm history-repair <id> --dry-run -> chain_drift_before false, entries_rehashed 0\n\nRepair correctly declines: the chain itself verifies end to end. The mismatch is between the last recorded after_hash and the hash of the item file on disk, because the merged field set was produced by the merge driver rather than by any recorded operation. No history entry describes it, no version addresses it, and pm restore cannot reproduce it. Every branch merge therefore leaves a permanent drift warning that no shipped command can clear, and pm validate reports ok true while carrying it.\n\nThis contradicts the append-only invariant directly: the merge is a mutation of tracked data, and the outcome milestone pm-w7ccmv requires restore-to-any-version and point-in-time reads to hold across merge. pm-76dnfg asserts a verifying chain after reanchor as a conformance property; this item owns the write-side primitive that property needs, namely recording the resolution as an entry whose patch is the merge outcome and whose provenance names the branches, drivers, and inputs it reconciled. pm-2sbj8p consumes it as evidence for the convergence model."
type: Task
status: closed
priority: 1
tags: []
created_at: "2026-07-25T20:40:33.139Z"
updated_at: "2026-07-31T14:23:59.324Z"
closed_at: "2026-07-27T00:28:49.685Z"
author: "harness:claude-code"
estimated_minutes: 480
acceptance_criteria: "The merge resolution is recorded as a history entry whose patch reproduces the merged item state exactly, so the last after_hash equals the hash of the merged item file and pm history --verify passes with no manual step; The entry carries merge provenance: the contributing stream heads or branch identities, the driver that produced the resolution, and per-field attribution for any field where the branches disagreed; pm restore and pm get --at can address the merged state like any other version, asserted by a test that merges divergent branches and then restores to the post-merge version from the stream alone; A clean merge leaves pm validate with zero history-drift warnings, and a genuine tamper still fails, so the drift signal keeps its meaning; history-repair keeps declining to rewrite a verifying chain: recording the resolution is the fix, and repair is not extended to fabricate entries; Recording is deterministic and order-independent, so merging the same branch set in different orders yields the same merged state and equivalent recorded provenance; The workspace-scope equivalent is covered or explicitly deferred with a reason: settings, schema, and relationship artifacts merged by the same fence get the same treatment"
parent: pm-o2kc
risk: high
confidence: 75
resolution: "pm merge reconcile now records receipt-backed merge_reconcile events for drifted and clean item streams, preserving replayable merged state with privacy-safe provenance; workspace settings/schema replay is explicitly deferred to pm-klo8."
expected_result: "Every field-aware item merge becomes an addressable, verifiable history state; workspace-scope handling is either implemented or explicitly routed to its canonical lineage."
actual_result: "The driver previously produced an unrecorded merged item state; settings/schema restore remains outside the shipped pm-klo8 workspace-history scope, while relationship streams already merge append-only."
